SwoopDAE null-latch crash (WinHint). CreatePhaseWithCFGLoads assumes that when the
loop latch ends in an unconditional branch, its single predecessor holds the exit
branch. After -single-loop-unroll of a body that ends in a guarded block (e.g. the
padding checks of contrast_mobilenet_infer's conv3x3_stem), the latch is the join
block of that guard: getSinglePredecessor() is null and Latch->getTerminator()
segfaults. Fall back to the loop's unique exiting block (the block with the exit
branch). BranchMerge's minimizeFunctionFromBranchPred makes the same choice so the
exit branch is never "reduced". PhaseStitching's getExitingBlock (placement of the
execute-phase end marker) has the same assumption; it falls back to the latch.
Applied by build.sh after 0001.

diff -ru a/projects/src/SWOOP/Transform/PhaseStitching.cpp b/projects/src/SWOOP/Transform/PhaseStitching.cpp
--- a/projects/src/SWOOP/Transform/PhaseStitching.cpp	2026-10-01 19:38:35.631817815 -0300
+++ b/projects/src/SWOOP/Transform/PhaseStitching.cpp	2026-10-01 19:38:35.682881958 -0300
@@ -151,6 +151,10 @@
 
   if (TI->getNumSuccessors() == 1) {
     executeBodyEnd = latch->getSinglePredecessor();
+    // WinHint: a latch that joins several paths has no single predecessor;
+    // place the phase-end marker in the latch itself instead of crashing.
+    if (!executeBodyEnd)
+      executeBodyEnd = latch;
   } else {
     executeBodyEnd = latch;
   }
